{"timestamp":"2026-05-19T17:57:55.547Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"{\"findings\":[{\"title\":\"Gemini transcript chunking reserializes through a lossy struct\",\"category\":\"data-loss\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/agent.go\",\"startLine\":56,\"endLine\":58,\"symbol\":\"Agent.ReassembleTranscript\",\"quote\":\"ReassembleTranscript combines chunks back into a single transcript.\"},{\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/transcript.go\",\"startLine\":220,\"endLine\":224,\"symbol\":\"NormalizeTranscript\",\"quote\":\"GeminiMessage only captures a subset of fields (id, type, content, toolCalls).\"},{\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/gemini.go\",\"startLine\":318,\"endLine\":350,\"symbol\":\"GeminiCLIAgent.ChunkTranscript\",\"quote\":\"var transcript GeminiTranscript\"},{\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/gemini.go\",\"startLine\":400,\"endLine\":411,\"symbol\":\"GeminiCLIAgent.ReassembleTranscript\",\"quote\":\"result, err := json.Marshal(GeminiTranscript{Messages: allMessages})\"},{\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/transcript.go\",\"startLine\":314,\"endLine\":327,\"symbol\":\"SliceFromMessage\",\"quote\":\"t, err := ParseTranscript(data)\"}],\"reasoning\":\"ChunkTranscript, ReassembleTranscript, and SliceFromMessage parse raw Gemini JSON into GeminiTranscript/GeminiMessage and then marshal that reduced model back out. The package itself documents that this model drops real transcript fields such as timestamp, model, and tokens. Any large transcript that is chunked and later reassembled, or any scoped transcript produced by SliceFromMessage, loses top-level metadata and per-message fields outside id/type/content/toolCalls, violating the reassembly contract and permanently degrading stored transcript fidelity.\",\"reproduction\":\"Create a Gemini transcript with top-level sessionId and a message containing timestamp, model, and tokens; call ChunkTranscript with a small maxSize and then ReassembleTranscript. The resulting JSON contains only messages with the GeminiMessage fields and omits sessionId/timestamp/model/tokens.\",\"recommendation\":\"Implement Gemini chunking and slicing over raw JSON: unmarshal the top-level object into map[string]json.RawMessage, split messages as []json.RawMessage, and preserve top-level fields plus raw message objects when reassembling. Only normalize content where explicitly required.\",\"whyTestsDoNotAlreadyCoverThis\":\"The existing round-trip test builds fixtures with GeminiTranscript, which cannot represent the fields being lost, and it only asserts message type/content/toolCalls.\",\"suggestedRegressionTest\":\"Add a forced-chunking round-trip test using raw JSON with sessionId plus message timestamp/model/tokens/thoughts, and assert those fields survive reassembly. Add a SliceFromMessage test with the same unknown fields.\",\"minimumFixScope\":\"Update GeminiCLIAgent.ChunkTranscript, GeminiCLIAgent.ReassembleTranscript, and SliceFromMessage to preserve raw JSON fields; broaden geminicli tests for unknown-field preservation.\"},{\"title\":\"InstallHooks can treat disabled or partial Gemini hooks as fully installed\",\"category\":\"bug\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/types.go\",\"startLine\":14,\"endLine\":17,\"symbol\":\"GeminiHooks\",\"quote\":\"Hooks are only executed when hooksConfig.enabled is true in .gemini/settings.json.\"},{\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/hooks.go\",\"startLine\":98,\"endLine\":100,\"symbol\":\"GeminiCLIAgent.InstallHooks\",\"quote\":\"hooksConfig.Enabled = true\"},{\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/hooks.go\",\"startLine\":126,\"endLine\":142,\"symbol\":\"GeminiCLIAgent.InstallHooks\",\"quote\":\"if existingCmd == expectedCmd\"},{\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/hooks.go\",\"startLine\":429,\"endLine\":440,\"symbol\":\"GeminiCLIAgent.AreHooksInstalled\",\"quote\":\"Check for at least one of our hooks\"},{\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/hooks_test.go\",\"startLine\":126,\"endLine\":145,\"symbol\":\"TestInstallHooks_Idempotent\",\"quote\":\"Second install should add 0 hooks\"}],\"reasoning\":\"The idempotency check only verifies that a SessionStart command matches the expected command, then returns before writing settings. If hooksConfig.enabled is missing or false, the in-memory assignment to true is never persisted, so Gemini still will not execute hooks. The same early return also leaves partial installations unrepaired when SessionStart exists but other lifecycle hooks are absent. AreHooksInstalled has the same weak predicate: any one managed hook is enough, regardless of hooksConfig.enabled or the full hook set.\",\"reproduction\":\"Write .gemini/settings.json with only the expected production SessionStart hook and either no hooksConfig or hooksConfig.enabled=false, then call InstallHooks(context.Background(), false, false). It returns 0 without adding the other 11 hooks or persisting hooksConfig.enabled=true.\",\"recommendation\":\"Make idempotency validate the full desired state: hooksConfig.enabled must be true and all expected managed hooks for the selected mode must be present. If any part differs, remove managed hooks and write the complete set. AreHooksInstalled should also require hooksConfig.enabled and the required hook set, or expose a separate health/repair check.\",\"whyTestsDoNotAlreadyCoverThis\":\"The idempotency test exercises only a clean full install followed by a second install. It does not cover a matching SessionStart with disabled hooksConfig or missing sibling hooks.\",\"suggestedRegressionTest\":\"Add tests for InstallHooks with an existing matching SessionStart but hooksConfig.enabled=false, and with only SessionStart present. Assert the call writes hooksConfig.enabled=true and installs all 12 hooks.\",\"minimumFixScope\":\"Revise GeminiCLIAgent.InstallHooks idempotency and GeminiCLIAgent.AreHooksInstalled completeness checks.\"},{\"title\":\"UninstallHooks suppresses non-missing read errors\",\"category\":\"bug\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/hooks.go\",\"startLine\":321,\"endLine\":325,\"symbol\":\"GeminiCLIAgent.UninstallHooks\",\"quote\":\"if err != nil { return nil }\"},{\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/hooks_test.go\",\"startLine\":402,\"endLine\":412,\"symbol\":\"TestUninstallHooks_NoSettingsFile\",\"quote\":\"Should not error when no settings file exists\"}],\"reasoning\":\"UninstallHooks treats every os.ReadFile failure as 'nothing to uninstall'. That is correct for os.ErrNotExist, but wrong for permission, transient I/O, or path errors: the command reports success while leaving managed hooks in place.\",\"reproduction\":\"On a Unix filesystem, create .gemini/settings.json with managed hooks, remove read permission from the file or directory, and call UninstallHooks. The function returns nil even though it could not inspect or remove the hooks.\",\"recommendation\":\"Return nil only when errors.Is(err, os.ErrNotExist). For other read errors, return a wrapped error so callers know uninstall did not complete.\",\"whyTestsDoNotAlreadyCoverThis\":\"The existing test covers only the missing-file case and does not simulate an unreadable existing settings file.\",\"suggestedRegressionTest\":\"Add an unreadable settings file or unreadable .gemini directory test on platforms that support chmod, skipping on unsupported platforms, and assert UninstallHooks returns an error.\",\"minimumFixScope\":\"Change the ReadFile error branch in GeminiCLIAgent.UninstallHooks and add targeted coverage.\"}],\"inspected\":{\"files\":[\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/discovery.go\",\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/gemini.go\",\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/generate.go\",\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/hooks.go\",\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/lifecycle.go\",\